  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The context",
      "long_title": false,
      "wrap": "pretty",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "style": "plain",
          "text": "Millions of Syrian refugee children were out of school, with no way to learn to read in their own language. In a context of low or no connection, how do we make literacy available and fun to all?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The question",
      "long_title": false,
      "wrap": "pretty",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "How might we make learning accessible?",
            "How might we make learning fun enough to distract from camp conditions?"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "What I did",
      "long_title": false,
      "wrap": "pretty",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Educational game design",
            "Pedagogical input",
            "Test and report"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "What changed",
      "long_title": false,
      "wrap": "pretty",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "We went from a static game that \"stores\" rigid reading skills in Arabic to an innovative method that is flexible to all languages.",
            "A game that adapts to the player's conditions."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "What I liked",
      "long_title": false,
      "wrap": "pretty",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "style": "quote",
          "text": "Mixing pedagogy and play."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "What I’d change",
      "long_title": false,
      "wrap": "pretty",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "style": "plain",
          "text": "[ADD]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "style": "plain",
          "text": "I would spend more time with the kids in various contexts (newcomers in camps, kids on the run, ...)"
        }
      ]
    },
